SUMMARY:The finitary aspects of Full Ground Local State (Orpheas van Rooij)
LOCATION:LG23\, Computer Science
DESCRIPTION:Orpheas van Rooij\nTheoretical Computer Science Seminar\n\nFull
  ground local state (FGLS) refers to dynamically allocated mutable state t
 hat allows storing ground values and references. It is a key ingredient in
  many imperative algorithms as it enables cyclic data structures. In this 
 work\, we focus on one particular denotational model for FGLS: Kammar et a
 l.'s possible worlds monad on sets indexed over sets of locations. We reso
 lve an outstanding question about this FGLS monad: is it finitary? We show
  that it is not\, by showing the existence of non-finitary computations in
  this monad that are challenging to define in a terminating language with 
 full ground references. This prompts us to introduce a finitary submonad o
 f Kammar et al.'s monad\, which…\n\nDetails: https://researchseminars.or
 g/talk/TheoryCSBham/90/
